@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+INP diagnostics run on every page load using the locally vendored Google
+`web-vitals` 5.1.0 attribution build. There are no analytics requests.
+
+Interact with the page and check the console for `[INP]` warnings when the page's
+INP exceeds 200 ms. Reports show the interaction target, input delay, event
+processing time, presentation delay, and overlapping script source locations
+and forced layout time when available. The largest phase suggests where to
+investigate; overlapping scripts are evidence to investigate, not proof of cause.
+
+From the console:
+
+```js
+inpDiagnostics.supported // Event Timing / interaction ID support
+inpDiagnostics.supportsLongFrames // detailed script attribution support
+inpDiagnostics.getReports() // latest 20 INP updates, JSON-safe copies
+inpDiagnostics.download() // save these reports as JSON
+```
+
+For an explicit monitoring integration, listen to the `inp-diagnostic` window
+event and read `event.detail`. No data is sent automatically. Reports omit input
+values and DOM nodes, but selectors and script URLs can contain identifying data;
+review them before forwarding reports to a service.
+
+These are updates to the page's INP candidate, not a log of every interaction.
+The library handles interaction grouping, outliers, backgrounding, and back/forward
+cache restores. The final page value may change as the session continues. Event
+durations are rounded by the browser. Browsers without Event Timing support
+produce no reports; browsers without Long Animation Frames still report timing
+phases but cannot identify scripts. Cross-origin frames and some script work
+cannot be attributed. A single local session is not a field percentile.
+
+To update the vendored dependency, update the pinned `web-vitals` version with
+pnpm, copy `node_modules/web-vitals/dist/web-vitals.attribution.js` into `vendor/`,
+and copy its `LICENSE` to `vendor/web-vitals.LICENSE`.
+
+References: https://web.dev/articles/inp and
+https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals#attribution
